          %h4#qft_duality_and_specifically_montonenolive_electricmagnetic_duality QFT Duality and specifically Montonen-Olive electric/magnetic duality
          %p
            By embedding quantum field theories in string theory (typically as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theories of various
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dualities of string theory
            will relate different QFTs in ways that are typically far from obvious from just looking at these QFTs themselves.
          %p
            The investigation specifically of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D1+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=1 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            in this fashion has come to be known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+quantum+field+theory"} geometric engineering of quantum field theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Montonen-Olive+duality"} Montonen-Olive duality
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"}> super
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            derives from conformal invariance of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-supersymmetric+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-supersymmetric QFT
            (see there)
