          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Strassler"}> Matthew Strassler
              ,
              %em Millenial Messages for QCD from the Superworld and from the String
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0309140"}> arXiv:hep-th/0309140
              )
          %h4#application_to_qcd_and_experimental_particle_physics Application to QCD and experimental particle physics
          %p
            The realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            that describes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and their interaction by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
            carried by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
            is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"}> QCD
            ).
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#QCDScatteringAmplitudes"} QCD Scattering amplitudes
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#QuarkGluonPlasma"} Quark-gluon plasma
          %h5#QCDScatteringAmplitudes Scattering amplitudes
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitudes"} string scattering amplitudes
            exhibit certain relations due to the extended nature of the string which are retained in the point particle limit and hence explain and serve to discover subtle relations in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT"} QFT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+string+theory"} twistor string theory
                explains some (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D4+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"}> super
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
            %li
              %p
                Precision scattering amplitudes in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
                use
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+string+theory"} twistor string theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell+recursion"} on-shell recursion
                methods,
          %p
            This also goes by the term “on-shell methods”. See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amplituhedron"} amplituhedron
          %p Reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Strassler"}> Matthew Strassler
                ,
                %em From string theory to the large hadron collider
                (
                %a{:href => "http://profmattstrassler.com/2012/08/15/from-string-theory-to-the-large-hadron-collider/"}> blog post
                )
            %li#Dixon13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lance+Dixon"}> Lance Dixon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculating Amplitudes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.preposterousuniverse.com/blog/2013/10/03/guest-post-lance-dixon-on-calculating-amplitudes/"} web
            %li
              %p
                Rutger Boels,
                %em On-shell recursion for string theory amplitudes on the disk and the sphere
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.itp.uni-hannover.de/nordic/slides/Boels.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p Original articles include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zvi+Bern"}> Zvi Bern
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lance+Dixon"} Lance Dixon
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kosower"} David Kosower
                %em On-Shell Methods in Perturbative QCD
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0704.2798"}> arXiv:0704.2798
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Strassler"} Matthew Strassler
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hard Scattering and Gauge/String Duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://lanl.arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0109174"} arXiv:hep-th/0109174
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#BDDPT19
              %p
                Johannes Broedel, Claude Duhr, Falko Dulat, Brenda Penante, Lorenzo Tancredi,
                %em Elliptic polylogarithms and Feynman parameter integrals
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.09971"}> arXiv:1902.09971
                )
              %p reviewed in
              %p
                Lorenzo Tancredi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Feynman integrals and higher genus surfaces
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/750565/"} Amplitudes 2019
                (
                %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/750565/contributions/3438642/attachments/1871838/3080501/Tancredi.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            See also below
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#GravityScattetingAmplitudes"} Application to gravity – Scattering amplitudes
          %h5#QuarkGluonPlasma Quark-gluon plasma
          %p
            Properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark-gluon+plasma"} quark-gluon plasma
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT-dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Pavel Kovtun,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quark-Gluon Plasma and String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.bnl.gov/rhic/news/091107/story2.asp"} blog entry
            %li
              %p
                Makoto Natsuume,
                %em String theory and quark-gluon plasma
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0701201"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0701201
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Gubser"}> Steven Gubser
                ,
                %em Using string theory to study the quark-gluon plasma: progress and perils
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0907.4808"}> arXiv:0907.4808
                )
          %h4#to_the_confinement_problem To the confinement problem
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Berman"}> David Berman
                , Maulik K. Parikh,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement and the AdS/CFT Correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://es.arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002031"} arXiv:hep-th/0002031
            %li
              %p
                Henrique Boschi Filho,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em AdS/QCD and confinement
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Workshop on Strongly Coupled QCD: The confinement problem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.if.ufrj.br/~boschi/pesquisa/seminarios/AdS_QCD_Confinement_UERJ_2011.pdf"} pdf
          %h4#to_super_yangmills_theory To super Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg+duality"} Seiberg duality
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            is conceptually explained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            on certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            configurations (…)
          %h3#ApplicationsToGravity Applications to gravity
          %h4#GravityScattetingAmplitudes Scattering amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open%2Fclosed+string+duality"} open/closed string duality
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitudes"} string scattering amplitudes
                allows to compute
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
                in terms of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
                scattering amplitudes: the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KLT+relations"} KLT relations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zvi+Bern"}> Zvi Bern
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Perturbative Quantum Gravity and its Relation to Gauge Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0206071"} arXiv:gr-qc/0206071
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.12942%2Flrr-2002-5"} doi:10.12942/lrr-2002-5
            %li
              %p
                more on this string-organizatioon of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering"} scattering
                amplitudes is in
              %p
                David C. Dunbar, Paul S. Norridge,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculation of Graviton Scattering Amplitudes using String-Based Methods
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9408014"} arXiv:hep-th/9408014
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KLT+relations"} KLT relations
                used for instance to demonstrate:
              %ul
                %li
                  multi-loop finiteness of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D8+d%3D4+supergravity"} N=8 d=4 supergravity
          %h4#GravitationalWaveSignatures Gravitational wave signatures
          %p
            On using
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KLT+relation"} KLT relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+copy"} double copy
            for computing
            = succeed "-signatures" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitational+wave"} gravitational wave
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+binary"} relativistic binary
            mergers for use with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LIGO"} LIGO
          %ul
            %li#BCRSSZ19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zvi+Bern"}> Zvi Bern
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Cheung"} Clifford Cheung
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radu+Roiban"} Radu Roiban
              = succeed "," do
                %em Scattering Amplitudes and the Conservative Hamiltonian for Binary Systems at Third Post-Minkowskian Order
              %strong 122
              201603 (2019) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.04424"}> arXiv:1901.04424
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.122.201603"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.122.201603
          %h4#black_hole_entropy Black hole entropy
          %p
            Semi-classical QFT computations suggest that there should be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            associated with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
          %p
            Since the quantum dynamics of general black holes is outside the reach of perturbative methods in string theory, certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} supersymmetric black hole
            solutions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            have properties independent of the coupling and are known to be the strong-coupling limit of what at weak coupling is a certain configuration of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            in flat space. Therefore the ordinary entropy of these brane configurations should match the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            of the corresponding black holes, and this has been confirmed to good precision.
          %p
            While this argument does not give direct information about the origin of the BH-entropy of physically observed black holes, it does show conceptually, in the general context of black holes in theories of gravity, BH-entropy can be accounted for by microscopic degrees of freedom in a theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
          %p Reviews include
          %ul
            %li#AGMOO
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ofer+Aharony"}> Ofer Aharony
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Gubser"} Steven Gubser
              = succeed "," do
